The runbook required the plane to be proved before capturing; it now carries the
transcript. Box IP control 203.0.113.1; the Tor-routed reader answered from
204.8.96.144 and check.torproject.org returned {"IsTor":true,"IP":"185.220.101.34"}.
Exits rotate per run (the two proofs differ), so neither is quoted as a current
state.

Scope stated in the runbook itself: this proves the SOCKS plane the runbook points
at, not REA's own CDP launch with those flags — that needs a REA capture invocation
this session did not run. The plan's P7.T2 line is closed with that caveat.
